index c4d1e07d..cf7b8258 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -28,15 +28,32 @@ Added glfw-3.4.bin.WIN64 to the vendor folder for OpenGL building to work.
 
 This seems to fix the glitchy audio that I was having before, I think it was possibly my lua setup that was causing it.
 
+I have disabled D3D9 and DirectX builds for this ReVC build, I didn't want to support both for ImGui and OpenGL works well on Linux, I'm not too worried about DirectX support for this ReVC.
+
+By default, this uses C++20 instead of C++11, but it runs fine with C++20 setup.
+
 ## ImGui info
 This project has an ImGui mod menu, which can be opened with `F8` on the keyboard, or `RB` + `A` on an Xbox controller.
 
 I got this building and running on Windows and Linux.
 Tested ImGui on my Steam deck and now it seems to work, I accidentally disabled the ImGui init for other platforms in glfw.cpp.
 
+You can toggle ImGui in the `reVC.ini`, if `ImGuiMenuToggle` is set to 0 it is off, and 1 is on.
+
 Librw is now added in as a submodule within the opengl-imgui branch
 * https://git.internal.kelsoncraft.net/kelson8/librw/src/branch/opengl-imgui/
 
+## Lua Info
+
+This ReVC project has a lua loader that loads custom lua scripts.
+
+Here is a list of info for the lua scripts
+[New files and additions](guides/file-changes.md#new-files-and-additions)
+
+There are some example scripts in `gamefiles/ViceExtended/lua_scripts`
+
+You can toggle Lua in the `reVC.ini`, if `LuaTest` is set to 0 it is off, and 1 is on.
+
 ## Docker support
 This branch now has support for building with Docker on Linux, tested on WSL with Ubuntu 24.04 and a Debian 13 server.
 
